aders or writers to finish, then sync the...","sourceKind":"general","title":"Checkpoint a database - SQLite","url":"https://sqlite.org/c3ref/wal_checkpoint_v2.html"},{"authoritative":false,"fetchRisk":"medium","score":0,"scoreReasons":["query_term_match"],"snippet":"The sqlite3_wal_checkpoint_v2 (D,X,M,L,C) interface runs a checkpoint operation on database X of database connection D in mode M. Status information is written back into integers pointed to by L and C. The M parameter must be a valid checkpoint mode: SQLITE_CHECKPOINT_PASSIVE Checkpoint as many frames as possible without waiting for any database readers or writers to finish, then sync the...","sourceKind":"general","title":"Checkpoint a database","url":"https://a1.sqlite.org/c3ref/wal_checkpoint_v2.html"},{"authoritative":false,"fetchRisk":"medium","score":0,"scoreReasons":["query_term_match"],"snippet":"Checkpoint as many frames as possible without waiting for any database readers or writers to finish, then sync the database file if all frames in the log were checkpointed. The busy -handler callback is never invoked in the SQLITE_CHECKPOINT_PASSIVE mode.","sourceKind":"general","title":"Checkpoint a database - sqlite.org","url":"http://www3.sqlite.org/c3ref/wal_checkpoint_v2.html"},{"authoritative":false,"fetchRisk":"medium","score":0,"scoreReasons":["query_term_match"],"snippet":"This is what happens: One connection does a checkpoint. This first checkpoint must be complete. In other words, the checkpoint must successfully copy all content from the WAL file back into the database and leave the WAL file in a state where it can potentially be reset. Shortly after the first checkpoint completes, a second checkpoint is started.","sourceKind":"general","title":"Write-Ahead Logging - SQLite","url":"https://sqlite.org/wal.html"}],"searchAttempts":[{"provider":"duckduckgo-web","resultCount":4,"status":"ok","url":"https://noai.duckduckgo.com/?q=site%3Asqlite.org%20WAL%20checkpoint%20busy"}],"searchProvider":"du